  "title": "How to Reduce Downtime in Manufacturing",
  "summary": "Most downtime reduction efforts start and stop at the machine level: fix the bearing, update the PM schedule, add a sensor. That is necessary work, but it only addresses part of the problem. The other part lives in the production system itself: a scheduling decision that starves a bottleneck station, a changeover sequence that no one has optimised in three years, a quality hold that stops a line for an hour because there is no process for fast disposition. These losses do not show up as equipme",
